{"storyRoleAssignments": [{"storyId": "AMSD-2041", "agentRole": "typescript-engineer"}], "profileAdditions": [{"role": "typescript-engineer", "rules": ["When implementing the Skyscanner API client, use the global fetch (Node 18+) directly — do NOT import from 'node-fetch' as a type source; this conflicts with global fetch types and causes TS7022 cascading type errors. Use `typeof globalThis.fetch` for typing if needed.", "When writing the manual process.argv CLI parser, use process.stderr.write() for all error/diagnostic output — NOT console.error. Tests will spy on process.stderr.write, and console.error writes to a different stream that breaks test assertions.", "When writing functions that return a union type (success | error result), ALWAYS add an explicit return type annotation. TypeScript cannot narrow untagged unions at call sites without explicit annotations, and strict mode will flag implicit any at consumer sites.", "When writing the CLI entry point (cli.ts) alongside a test file (cli.test.ts) in the same story, write the test file FIRST. Writing implementation first risks running out of context before tests are written, leaving the story in an untested state.", "When using vi.stubGlobal to mock fetch in test files, always type the mock parameters explicitly — e.g. `vi.stubGlobal('fetch', vi.fn<(url: string, init?: RequestInit) => Promise<Response>>())`. Untyped mock parameters trigger noImplicitAny errors under strict mode.", "When parsing numeric query parameters or CLI args (e.g. --adults), always narrow the type explicitly: `const adults = parsedArgs.adults ? Number(parsedArgs.adults) : 1`. Passing `number | undefined` where `number` is required will fail strictNullChecks.", "When writing the Skyscanner API response types, define them as exported interfaces with exact field names matching the live API response shape. The paired test story will import these types — any mismatch in field names between the type and the mock response will cause compile errors in the test file.", "NEVER hardcode API keys, tokens, or secrets in any source file — not even as placeholders. Use `process.env.RAPIDAPI_KEY` or `process.env.SKYSCANNER_API_KEY` patterns. Any string matching `/sk-[a-z]+-[a-zA-Z0-9]+/` or resembling a credential will trigger a SAST blocker.", "NEVER modify package.json, tsconfig.json, vitest.config.ts, or any scaffold-phase infrastructure file. These are owned by the scaffold phase and are immutable. If a change appears needed, flag it as a blocker instead.", "When writing the contract file for this story, include the exact Skyscanner API client class constructor signature, the searchFlights method signature with all parameter field names, and a ready-to-paste vi.mock() factory showing the exact import path and call pattern."]}, {"role": "sast-sentinel", "rules": ["Authorized source files for findings: only files returned by `find . -name '*.ts' -not -path '*/node_modules/*'` in the project root. Any finding referencing a file not in this list MUST be suppressed as a hallucination.", "Test file naming convention: *.test.ts in src/. A function tested in any *.test.ts file in src/ counts as covered — do not report missing tests for a function that has a test in any test file in src/.", "NEVER report findings about non-existent files or files outside the authorized list. Cross-reference every file path in your findings against the actual file list before emitting.", "NEVER flag the use of process.env.* patterns as hardcoded secrets — these are the correct pattern. Only flag literal strings matching credential patterns like /sk-[a-z]+-[a-zA-Z0-9]+/."]}, {"role": "review-ranger", "rules": ["Authorized exported symbols: only symbols returned by `grep -rn '^export' src/ --include='*.ts'` exist in this project. Any finding about an untested function MUST reference a symbol from this list — findings about non-existent functions are hallucinations and must be suppressed.", "Test file naming convention: *.test.ts in src/. A function tested in any *.test.ts file in src/ counts as covered — not just a dedicated test file. Do not report a function as untested if any test file in src/ imports and exercises it.", "Before reporting 'function X is untested', verify that X is in the exported symbols list AND that no *.test.ts file in src/ references it. Both conditions must be true for the finding to be valid."]}, {"role": "spec-validator", "rules": ["Test file naming convention for this project: *.test.ts in src/. When validating test coverage against acceptance criteria, accept tests from any *.test.ts file in src/ — not just a dedicated file per function.", "Source files are located in src/ and follow the pattern src/**/*.ts. Test files are co-located in src/ as *.test.ts. Do not expect a separate __tests__ directory."]}, {"role": "mutant-hunter", "rules": ["Test file naming convention: *.test.ts in src/. When computing mutation coverage, include all *.test.ts files in src/ as the test corpus — not just files matching a dedicated naming pattern.", "Source files are in src/**/*.ts. Do not attempt mutation testing on files in node_modules/, dist/, or configuration files."]}], "newProfiles": []}
